        "details": "Each trial draws paired team baselines, selects one team per pair by a fair coin, adds the stipulated labour and retention effects, and adds measurement error. The decision uses the resulting paired differences. With 96 teams, 15,459 trials passed the labour criterion and 19,990 passed the retention criterion. In the central design, each team has standard normal latent labour and quality values with correlation 0.3. Within a pair the latent values for a given outcome have correlation 0.7. A latent labour value z maps to baseline hours per initial unit 3 + 7 exp(0.35 z − 0.35²/2). A latent quality value z maps to baseline retention 0.72 + 0.25/(1 + exp(−1.4 z)). Pair differences receive independent zero-mean Gaussian measurement errors with standard deviations sqrt(2) times 0.2 hours per initial unit and sqrt(2) times 0.005 in retained fraction. No pair is lost in the central scenario. The one-sided paired Student t bounds allow 0.2 hours per initial unit and one percentage point for differential bias."
      }
    }
    require role == "backing"
  }

  evidence scope_conditions {
    kind argument_material
    environment engineering_work
    max_age 315360000
    derive material
    input {
      "material": {
        "role": "scope",
        "classification": "Conditions for applying this inference",
        "details": "The rates concern hypothetical team-level outcomes. The simulator draws no individual tasks or forecasts, and the planned twenty tasks per team enter the collection budget only. Random simulation error and uncertainty about whether real teams resemble the simulated teams are separate sources of uncertainty."
      }
    }
    require role == "scope"
  }

  assumption applicability {
    statement "The rates concern hypothetical team-level outcomes. The simulator draws no individual tasks or forecasts, and the planned twenty tasks per team enter the collection budget only. Random simulation error and uncertainty about whether real teams resemble the simulated teams are separate sources of uncertainty."
    environment engineering_work
    validate scope_conditions
  }

  reasoning warrant {
