    rationale "Each simulated trial has a known true benefit. The fraction meeting both criteria estimates the probability of detecting that benefit under the chosen assumptions. The design requires the lower 95% Monte Carlo limit on detection to reach 90% in every required benefit scenario. Central pass rates of 44.79% and 77.25% fall short."
